course: dictionary
lesson: 6126
title: Midsummer
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: Midsummer is the middle of summer. It falls around the longest day of the year, when the sun is up for the most hours. You can use it as a noun, naming a time, or as an adjective, describing a noun.
explain: «Around midsummer the sky over Britain never gets fully dark.» The words around midsummer tell you it is a time of year, not one day on a calendar. Ask yourself: is this a time, a place or a thing? Here it is a time.
explain: Midsummer can also describe something. In «A Midsummer Night's Dream», midsummer tells you what kind of night it is. Read the words next to it to see if it names something or describes it.
fact: Midsummer means the middle of summer, around the longest day of the year.
fact: As a noun, midsummer names a time: «It is midsummer, so the night is short.»
fact: As an adjective, midsummer describes a noun: «A Midsummer Night's Dream» is a play with fairies.
fact: Midsummer Day and Midsummer's Eve are traditional festivals, especially in northern Europe.
fact: At Stonehenge, the stones line up with the sunrise at midsummer.
exercise: «Around midsummer the sky over Britain never gets fully dark.» What does midsummer mean here? | *The middle of summer, around the longest day | The middle of winter, around the shortest day | A kind of summer bird | A cold night in early spring
exercise: «It is midsummer, so the night is short.» Find and copy one word that tells you the time of year. | short | the | night | *midsummer
exercise: In «A Midsummer Night's Dream», what kind of word is midsummer? | noun | *adjective | adverb | verb
test: What does midsummer mean? | A type of bonfire | *The middle of summer, around the longest day of the year | The first day of autumn | A festival held in the middle of winter
test: «Ivana Kupala is an old midsummer night festival with flower wreaths and bonfires.» What do young people do at this festival? | *Jump over the fires | Plant trees in the fields | Sing in a choir | Swim across a lake
exam: In «It is midsummer, so the night is short», is midsummer a noun? | No, it describes a noun, so it is an adjective | No, it is a place | *Yes, it names the time of year | No, it is a verb
